      "attributes": {
        "id": 1008,
        "body_ja": null,
        "body": "<p>あわよくば is a combination of the old-fashioned い-Adjective あわよい 'convenient', 'timely', and the conjunction particle ば 'if'. It can be translated as 'if the time is right', 'if possible', or 'if luck is on my side'. Despite its roots, あわよくば is treated as a single word in modern Japanese, and is used in the same way as a typical adverb.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>あわよくば will come before a phrase expressing a desirable outcome.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155327'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155328'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155329'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='funfact'><h4>Fun Fact</h4>\r\n<p>Notice that ば attaches to the く form of the い-Adjective あわよい rather than けれ, as would usually be required with modern conjugation rules. This is due to the conjugation rules for ば in relation to い-Adjectives being different in both classical and modern Japanese.</p></section>"
